course: dictionary
lesson: 11118
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The words around it, its context, show you which meaning the writer wants. «The Mole was spring-cleaning with brooms, dusters and a pail of whitewash (a white paint for walls).» Here whitewash is a paint, and the brackets even tell you so.
explain: Sometimes you must work harder. «The report tried to whitewash the mistakes.» Mistakes are bad things, and a report that tries to make them disappear is hiding them. So here whitewash means to hide the bad things so they look innocent.
explain: In sport, a whitewash is a win where the other team scores nothing. «The home team won 5–0, a total whitewash.» Try each meaning in the sentence. Paint does not fit a score, but a win with no goals for the losers does.
fact: Whitewash is a white liquid made of lime or chalk and water, painted on walls and fences.
fact: As a verb, to whitewash means to paint something with whitewash, or to hide the bad things someone has done.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole is whitewashing his home when spring calls him, and he flings the brush down, saying «Bother!» and «O blow!»
fact: In Tom Sawyer, Tom tricks his friends into whitewashing a fence for him.
fact: In sport, a whitewash is a win where the losers score nothing or lose every game, as in «a 5–0 whitewash».
exercise: «The Mole was spring-cleaning with brooms, dusters and a pail of whitewash.» What is whitewash here? | A kind of broom | * A white paint for walls | A small, dark room | A type of cloth
exercise: «The report tried to whitewash the mistakes.» What does whitewash mean here? | To fix the mistakes quickly | * To hide the bad things so they look innocent | To paint the mistakes white | To count every mistake carefully
exercise: Ben says, «The home team won 5–0, a total whitewash.» What does whitewash mean? | A team that wears white shirts | * A win where the losers score nothing | A game called off because of rain | A draw with no goals at all
test: In The Wind in the Willows, what does Mole do with the brush when spring calls him? | * Flings it down | Uses it to wash his face | Gives it to Toad | Hangs it on the wall
test: In Tom Sawyer, what job does Tom trick his friends into doing? | Digging a pond | Washing the dog | * Whitewashing a fence | Cooking supper
exam: Read: «The politician's speech was a whitewash that fooled nobody.» What does whitewash most likely mean? | * The speech hid the truth so the bad things looked innocent | The speech made everyone laugh | The speech was painted white | The speech was very short and quiet
